	'nuances' => array(
        'INDUSTRY STYLE (native technical editor): Claims: say only what the English proves. No 最/第一/顶尖/卓越/革命性 unless the source has it; industry-leading = 行业领先, never 业界第一. Headings and CTAs are short verb-object phrases with no 。 or ！ (申请报价, 获取报价, 咨询专家, 下载宣传册). Spec labels are nouns (整机质量, 外形尺寸); table values are 是/否/选配/标配. Units: keep the source unit and figure exactly — an imperial figure keeps ″ (18″ × 30″, never 18 英寸) and gains no conversion (never （457 × 762 mm）). Write SI symbols after a half-width space (16 kg, 200 L/min, 29 bar, 10 N·m, g·mm), never 千克/巴/升/克·毫米. Use decimal points (0.75), en-dash ranges (40–420 mm), and 7×24 小时 for 24/7. Undo English syntax: put the condition first (如需…，请…), drop filler 它/进行/能够 but keep an ownership 我们的; 旗下 is only for brands, subsidiaries or sites (our many brands = 旗下众多品牌), never equipment or services (自有的 54 台 CNC 铣削中心), avoid 被 passives and 通过……从而…… chains, and use no more than two 的 per noun phrase. Slashes are always half-width /, never ／: spaced in spec labels and between figures (带 / 不带皮带传动, 1200 mm / 1500 mm), unspaced in prose and inside a Latin run (多托盘/多工位, 12V/24V); brand and model names in source case (DATAMES, Winbal); Image 1 → 图 1. One term per concept: 动平衡机 (not 平衡机), 试验台 (not 测试台) for a stand or bench but 测试 for every "X Test" product and test system (HST 测试系统, never 试验系统), 校正 for unbalance correction (not 修正), 单平面/双平面 for planes, 马达 for hydraulic and 电机 for electric, 标定 for ECU/ADAS/turbo parameter setting and propulsion/powertrain end-of-line calibrations, 校准 for instruments.',
        'Convert English nominalisations and passives into Chinese verb phrases and active voice (new possibilities → 开辟新的可能), but an "opportunity to do X" keeps the opportunity as its head: "customers have new opportunities to collect data" is 客户有了采集数据的新机遇, never 客户可采集数据，获得新的机遇. Avoid 被 unless the agent matters, never coin a noun absent from real Chinese industry writing, and never attach concrete adjectives to abstractions (可能性、机会).',
        'Consistency: one English term or label gets ONE Chinese rendering, identical on every surface (nav, H1, body, spec table, FAQ, card, footer, form, alt text, <title>, meta). Take the canonical form from the nav or footer and reuse it. Pick ONE rendering per term and per connector site-wide: 监测 (not 监控), 集成 (not 整合), 装配 (not 组装), 基地 (not 工厂) for a company site but 地点 for a UI or form field "Location", 表单 (not 表格), 与 (not 和) for "&" in nav labels. CNC stays Latin (CNC 铣削, never 数控铣削); gloss an acronym as 中文全称（缩写） on first mention only, then hold one form. Translate every parallel SET as a set: Previous/Next on one noun axis (上一个/下一个), every option in one <select> in the same language, all siblings nominalised if one is, either all bullets and spec rows ending in 。 or none (headings and CTAs take none), and a fragment keeps the source final mark ("...adding balancing weights etc.," ends 平衡块等，, never 等。), every placeholder using ……, never ASCII "...". A cut-off teaser translates only the shown words and ends on one …… (Designed… = 设计用于……).',
        'A spec-table or card label copies the English label\'s shape and adds nothing: End Drive (H2W) is 端部驱动（H2W）, not 端部驱动型（H2W）; U-axis control capability is U 轴控制能力, not 功能; "1 or 2 plane" is 单平面或双平面, never the clipped 单面; universal applicability is 通用性强; "Flows to 200 L/min" is 流量最高达 200 L/min. Keep the source\'s own head noun: an assembly is 组件／总成 (not 装配件), a component is 零部件 (not 工件). Recast a long English sentence into short Chinese clauses instead of tracking its syntax — do not chain 以…以…, do not end on 使…现代化 or 为…提供动力, and do not build a noun out of a purpose phrase: "Minimizes rework by catching system issues before assembly" is 在装配前发现系统问题，将返工降至最低, not 通过在装配前发现系统问题来最小化返工. Start on the circumstance and end on the assertion; do not calque maximize/minimize as a transitive verb (最大化设备价值 → 充分释放设备价值) and keep 性能 for machines only (business performance takes 业绩／效能／潜能); and prefer 了解 for Discover/See how, reserving 探索 for Explore.',
        'FIDELITY: never add, drop, strengthen or weaken a claim, modifier, number, qualifier or modality. "Addresses manufacturing process deficiencies" is 应对生产工艺缺陷, never 消除, but "eradicates all known weaknesses" IS 彻底消除 — render the verb the source wrote; "configured with or without X to meet specific requirements" is a neutral choice, 可根据特定要求选择配置或不配置 X, never 如有特定要求可配置 X; a generic "under pressure" is 在压力之下, never narrowed to 工期紧迫. Superlatives survive, modals survive as 可／能／有助于, and no 率、度、倍 the English does not state may appear. Hold the narrow technical sense in thermal and rotating-machinery copy: "vapor" in a thermodynamic cycle is 蒸气, never 蒸汽 (steam); automotive "turbo" is always 涡轮增压器 while bare 涡轮 means turbine and belongs to aerospace and jet-engine contexts; in turbocharger contexts "core" is the cartridge 芯体 (涡轮增压器芯体), never 芯轴 and never 铁芯.',
        'Press releases and executive bios follow Chinese newswire convention, not English sentence order: the dateline lead names the company FIRST with the descriptor in apposition, one fixed string in every release and card (2026 年 3 月 31 日——Ascential Technologies，全球领先的自动化诊断、检测、装配与测试系统及服务提供商，业务覆盖广泛的……), a Division is 事业部 (never 部门) and the division name Test & Measurement Systems is translated, 测试与测量系统事业部 (only the lockup Ascential Test & Measurement stays Latin), a career line reads 此前曾任／离任前担任, never 最近担任, an award or programme name sits inside 中文引号（“集成化产品方案奖”）.',
        '应用领域 is the NAV CATEGORY label only; mid-sentence it renames the product. A tagline "for <X> applications" is always 适用于 X 领域 (for fluid power rotary motion applications = 适用于流体传动旋转运动领域), and "What applications is X used for?" is X 有哪些应用？, never 适用于哪些应用. A FAQ "What is/are X?" asks for a definition: 什么是 X？, never X 有哪些？.',
        'Take a generic noun\'s shop-floor sense; never let a legal, medical, IT or office sense leak in: a valve "section" is 阀片 (never 条款), an EDT/EDM "generator" is 脉冲电源 (never 发电机), "injectors" are 充注头, "supervision" is 监视 (never 监督／监管), a counted "unit", machine or machining center takes 台 (54 台 CNC 铣削中心, never 个／单位), a factory "cell" is 工位／生产单元 (never 单元格), a "line" is 生产线 (never 行), "machine down" is 设备停机 (never 宕机), roll "texturing" is 毛化 (never 纹理化／粗化), a support "case" is 工单 (never 案例). In a hydraulic, agricultural or aerospace parts list "motor" is 马达; only an electric motor is 电机. Likewise 数据 not 输入, 检出率 not 检测机会, 挂车 not 拖车, 任务关键型 not 关键任务型.',
        'Event lines: "May 20, 2025 · Stuttgart, Germany, Booth 1637" is 2025 年 5 月 20 日 · 德国斯图加特，1637 展位; expand US state abbreviations (FL 佛罗里达州) and keep the fair brand in Latin (Automechanika 2026).',
        'Copy spec-table figures, never re-key them — a European decimal comma becomes a point (0,75 kW → 0.75 kW), the header "No." counts items (数量, never 编号), a "Value" column header is 数值 (never 价值), "with standard bed" is 采用标准床身时 (never 标准床身下), an electrical "16A connection" is 16 A 电源接口 (space before A/V/Hz, never 连接), "phase" in a rating is 相数, never 相位, and 1ph and 3 ph are 单相 and 三相, never 1 相 or 3 相.',
        'Cap any pre-nominal modifier at roughly 12 Chinese characters and never stack three 的 in one chain. Name the head noun FIRST and hang modifiers behind it instead of stacking every English post-modifier in front: "Engine cooling fan with motor balancing machine" is 带电机的发动机冷却风扇动平衡机. A product NAME ending "for <object>" is a compact compound with no 面向／用于 (Vertical Balancing Machines for Tools and Tool Holders = 刀具与刀柄立式动平衡机), identical in H1, alt text and FAQ; 面向……的 is for running prose only, and a long chain splits into a predicate clause (设备健康分析由打造这些测试系统的团队直接提供). Fold an English post-nominal example INSIDE the Chinese modifier (our brands, like Burke Porter → 包括 Burke Porter 在内的众多品牌), and give a bare gerund object its head noun (Elevating Support → 提升支持水平) without inventing a second clause — 提升支持，增进价值 adds a promise the source never made. Keep each asserted attribute as its own predicate (贴近客户、快速响应). 该 takes only a bare noun (该系统); a modified noun takes 这一 (这一互联式性能管理解决方案, never 该互联的…).',
        'Two taxonomy tags joined by an English comma take 、, not a dash: "Balancing, Transportation" is 动平衡、交通运输, never 动平衡——交通运输. Inside a 、 list join the parts of ONE item with 及／与, never 、 (输入与输出转速及扭矩仪表), and never nest a 、 list in a 、 list: move the inner items into （） (支持多种质量校正方式（铣削、钻削、焊接等）); a shared head noun covers both nouns (Conveyor and Paper Rolls = 输送辊与纸辊); a " - " title separator stays a spaced half-width hyphen (辅助阀测试 - Ascential Test & Measurement). In alt text translate every descriptive word: "on a transparent background" is 透明背景. Use written positional words (上方的).',
        'A rename copula is neither a launch nor an ownership statement — "is now a product brand under X" is 现已成为 X 旗下的产品品牌, and 现已推出 is reserved for an actual NOW AVAILABLE product. Never add a head noun (平台／工具／导航／技术) to a heading or label that names only a capability: "Analytics that deliver timely insights" is 提供及时洞察的数据分析.',
		'Keep a neutral verb neutral and never rhetorically upgrade a flat one. "can significantly impact downtime, machine health and repairs" is 对停机、设备健康状况与维修产生显著影响 — never split it into 减少停机、改善健康、优化维修; "is a promise and our standard" is 既是承诺，也是我们的标准, not the 不仅……更是 escalation.',
		'Never downgrade a claim verb or swap a named capability for a neighbouring one. "predict failures" is 预测故障／预判故障 with the object kept, and 预警 is allowed only where the English says alert/warn/notify; 诊断 stays 诊断 (not 提示), 检测 stays 检测 (not 提醒).',
		'Never change the noun a statistic counts, and give every counter its measure word. Countries stays 国家 (not 市场), people 人才／人员 (not 团队), locations 基地 (not 市场). Counter labels are numerals at runtime even though the HTML shows 0, so write 个国家, 名专业人才, 个全球基地, never the bare noun; "home countries" is 个所在国家 (never 扎根国家, never add 团队／办事处); when listed parts make up a total, join them with 包括, never 另有 ("56 locations across 18 facilities and 38 field agents" = 共 56 个服务网点，包括 18 个基地和 38 名现场服务代表); "years of innovation" is 年创新历程 (never bare 年创新).',
		'Keep every modifier and every relation the English states. Trailing purpose phrases survive ("for their consumers" = 为其消费者); a duration adverbial stays on the verb the English attaches it to; and the agent of a "for/from" noun phrase survives ("support requests for Bauer customers and other partners" means requests FROM them: Bauer 客户及其他合作伙伴提交的支持请求, not 对……的支持请求).',
		'Every Chinese verb needs its object, and every verb-object pair must be one that occurs in real Chinese industry writing. "allowing us to adapt swiftly" is 使我们能够迅速应变, never the objectless 迅速适应 — 适应、响应、提升、改善、满足 all require a stated object even where English drops it, and an English prepositional tail needs its own clause. Use 应对／迎接挑战 (never 解决挑战), 并肩同行 (never a clause ending on bare 并肩), 解决难题, 满足需求, 积累经验, 开展检测, 优化流程／配置 (never 优化需求), 缩短处理时间 (never 改善…时间), 交付智能系统并为其提供支持 for "deliver and support systems" (支持 + a product object reads as "endorse"); do not coordinate unlike categories under one verb just because English does — give each object a verb it takes (预防碰撞和保障道路安全, never 预防碰撞与道路安全); and a Chinese machine 做 a motion, it does not 执行 one. Feature-list items share one verb-object shape (以及符合 ISO 21940-23:2012 安全标准, never 以及安全标准符合……); give each listed action a verb it takes (核查运行状况，开展健康检查和校准).',
		'Never repeat the same morpheme inside one clause or label, and break a collision by changing the HEAD NOUN rather than the register. 无损检测 already IS non-destructive testing, so "NDT inspection" is 无损检测（NDT）, never 无损检测（NDT）检测; "Support & consulting sales inquiry" is 支持与咨询业务销售咨询.',
		'Delete the second marker and the perfective 了 when the clause does not need them: 在故障发生前预警, never 在故障发生前提前预警; 简化验证流程、提高吞吐量, not 简化了…、提高了….',
		'A "Where X, Y" opener takes 在: 在别人看到局限之处，我们…, never a bare 别人看到局限之处. Never open a Chinese sentence with a bare 或 copied from an English "Or ..." sentence — use 或者，… or fold the clause into the preceding sentence — and never open with a subjectless participial clause: "In a strategic move reflecting its commitment to X, Y announced…" is 作为一项战略举措，Y 宣布……，彰显其……的一贯承诺。 Never stack the frame in front of 举措／方案 or recast it as 为体现…….',
		'Rewrite English word order into Chinese shape. A "someone who" clause becomes 有人 + verb (都有人信赖它, never 都有一个相信……的人); "our complete range of X" is 我们全系列的 X (never 我们完整系列的). Questions and headings go topic-comment: "What\'s new at X?" is the noun phrase X 最新动态. Job titles are strictly left-branching, unit first, and a business segment takes 业务 so it cannot read as a trade or a technology: "CTO of Transportation" is 交通运输业务首席技术官, "Vice President of Technology, Aerospace & Industrials" is 航空航天与工业业务技术副总裁 (never 部门), but a Latin brand unit takes no 业务 (Ascential Care 销售副总裁); a region follows the segment and takes 区 (航空航天与工业业务美洲区域总监, 美洲区服务经理), and Marketing in a title is 市场 (市场经理, never 营销). A US town gets a Chinese name, Latin in （） (三河城（Three Rivers）基地). Appointment headlines map the verb one-to-one: Appoints/Names X as = 任命 X 为, Hires X as = 聘任 X 为, Promotes X to = 提拔 X 为 (晋升 is intransitive, only X 晋升为 Y with the person as subject; never 晋升 X 为, never 任命 X 晋升为), Collaborates with X for Y = 与 X 就 Y 业务开展合作 (never a dangling 面向 Y), Welcomes X as = 欢迎 X 加盟，出任. Degrees rebuild as 在<机构>取得<专业><学位> with established names (Master of Science in X = X 理学硕士), and a person takes a full Latin name on first mention then the established transliteration — never a bare Latin surname as the subject of a Chinese sentence.',
		'A one-word English nav category is often a clipped technical compound — expand it to the full Chinese industry term, and keep wayfinding labels plain and literal: "Power" alone is 动力 (动力总成 only for Powertrain), "Vision" in an inspection menu is 机器视觉, "Locations" is 全球基地 (never 全球布局). When "machine" modifies data or analytics, translate the OBJECT (设备健康分析, never 机器分析).',
		'Read service-offer wording against the commercial model. "Contract balancing as-a-service" is 委托动平衡即服务（BaaS）, because 合同 is the paper contract and 合同动平衡 parses as "balancing of a contract", while unqualified "balancing-as-a-service" stays 动平衡即服务. "Available X" in a menu of purchasable options goes predicate-final: 多种服务级别协议可选, not 可选服务级别协议 (readable as "the SLA is optional") and never 可用, which misparses as an availability (uptime) SLA.',
		'Keep the engineering colour of a verb used by an engineering company, and use a neutral adverb for corporate capability. "we engineer new, fast, precise and uncompromising possibilities" is 我们以工程技术开创全新、快速、精准、毫不妥协的可能, never bare 开创／打造, and never mix a 的-phrase (新的) with bare adjectives in one series; "from the team that builds the test systems" is 由打造这些测试系统的团队直接提供, never 亲自提供. Never translate a hortative CTA with 让我们 plus a verb: "Let\'s talk" is 洽谈合作, "Let\'s get started" is 立即开始, "Join us" is 加入我们.',
		'Form microcopy is written as native Chinese UI, not as translated English sentences. A <select> placeholder "Select an option" is 请选择 (never 选择一个选项); "Any error codes from the system you can share?" is 可否提供系统报出的错误代码？; "select from the forms below" keeps the choosing, 从下方选择相应表单填写, never 填写下方表单. In a chat or contact widget "message" is 消息, never 信息, and every input placeholder takes 请 plus a verb (请输入您的姓名), except a search box: 搜索产品……. A lead-in before an inline phone number ends on 致电: "You can phone us for sales assistance at" is 如需销售协助，请致电, never 您可致电我们，电话：.',
		'Translate EVERY string a cookie/consent component prints: table headers (名称／域名／有效期), 项 Cookie, every aria-label (Cookie consent → Cookie 同意设置), durations in Chinese units (2 年, 30 分钟, session = 会话期间). Controls go verb-first (Google Analytics Opt Out = 退出 Google Analytics 跟踪).',
		'aria-label landmarks: Primary = 主导航, Mobile primary = 移动端主导航, Sidebar = 侧边栏.',
		'Named offerings are brands even when every word looks translatable. If a phrase is a product or service name in a nav, footer product column or menu card (ADAS Garage, XL Machine, Lismar, Titan, WinterPark, Ascential Care), keep the WHOLE name in Latin script. Never half-translate a brand in one place and keep it in another on the same page, never attach ™ to a translated phrase, and when a label wraps a brand in <span class="tmm-brand-word">, ONLY the brand belongs inside that span.',
		'Translate an English abbreviation for a generic role, activity or object — Chinese readers mis-expand it (SME reads as 中小企业, PM as 项目经理): SME is 领域专家, PM (maintenance) 预防性维护, MUT 被测电机, DUT 被测件, BEMF 反电动势 (this overrides the base rule on bare acronyms). Keep Latin only for acronyms Chinese engineers write in Latin (NVH, ADAS, CAN, UDS, TCP, ERP, PLC).',
		'Place Chinese frames where Chinese grammar puts them. 作为……的一部分 opens the sentence before its subject (作为端到端支持服务的一部分，我们……, never 我们作为……的一部分); "A is integral to B" keeps A as subject (workport flow is integral to the HST = 工作油口流量通常封闭在 HST 内部，无法测量); "sizes range from X to Y" is 规格从 X 到 Y 不等, never 覆盖从面向…用…的系统; a qualifier on the last list item (as required, if equipped) stays on that item (…以及按需测试壳体泄油流量和清洁度), never fronted where it governs the whole list ("adds first alert monitoring and scheduling optimization based on usage data" = 新增早期预警监测，以及基于实际使用数据的排程优化); "regardless of location" attaches to the benefit it conditions. A subject "The system" is 该系统, because bare 系统 before a verb fuses into the noun 系统测试 (该系统用于测试装配正确性、机械效率…). Hold the source voice: we/our stays 我们/我们的 ("As a specialist, we also produce… Our balancers" = 我们还生产……我们的动平衡机), except that "At <Company>, we…" makes the company the subject, and "our" services stay 我们的 ("XL Machine provides more value through our assembly services" = XL Machine 通过我们的装配服务提供更多价值, never 旗下装配服务).',
		'Drop English service-marketing calques: "customers can expect X" is 客户可获得／均能享有 X (never 可期待), "at every step of their journey" is 在每个环节 (never 旅程), "actionable information" is 可付诸行动的信息 (never 可指导行动的), "now united under one roof" is 现已归于同一旗下 (never 汇聚于同一旗下, 整合为一体 or 同一屋檐之下), a list closing "and beyond"/"and more" ends on 等 (泄漏检测等, never ，以及更多), and a relative clause keeps its causal link (服务体验，从而创造……价值).',
		'In a service-plan or price matrix a short cell is a value of its row label, and every repeated label is character-identical in each table: a shipping priority "Next" is 下一班次 and "Next day" 次日 (never the pager 下一个), a "Preferred" tier is 优惠／优惠费率 (never 优选) and "Discounted" is 折扣／折扣费率 (never 优惠), labor and labour are both 人工, training "update & refresh" is 更新与巩固. A frequency tier cell is 年度／半年度 (Semi-annual (update & refresh) = 半年度（更新与巩固）), an included visit is 含每年／每半年一次上门服务 (never 出行), and a clipped label reuses the noun of its full row name (Review under Training review = 回顾, never 评审). Every cell gets a translation, however short.',
		'Use Simplified characters (简体), never Traditional, and full-width punctuation after every Chinese character — including a string-final colon before a phone or email link (获取现场支持：) and a clause comma (填写，我们) — never half-width : or , there: ，。、；：？！, curly quotes “ ” and （） — even when the English source shows ASCII " \' ( ). Half-width characters appear only inside an untranslated Latin run; a lone generic word (website, page) is translated (网站). Use 《》 for a document title before 白皮书. A spec label never keeps @ or a spaced –: "Accuracy – MU 60 runs @ 95% 2 standard deviations" is 精度：MU，60 次运行，95%（2 个标准差）. A category name inside ANY UI sentence always takes “ ”, in every sibling string: "Show 8 subcategories under Balancing Machines" is 显示“动平衡机”下的 8 个子类别, never 显示动平衡机下的. A colon title embedded in a sentence puts its subtitle in （）: 如需就驱动电机试验台（电机精密测试）获取定制报价, never a mid-sentence ：.',
		'Insert a single half-width space only where real Latin text or digits sit next to Chinese (使用 API 接口) — never around an inline <span> or <a> inside a Chinese sentence (将一切<span>融为一体</span>).',
		'Numbers use Western digits with a comma thousands separator exactly as the source writes them (15,000 r/min, never 15 000), currency 1,500 元, dates 2026 年 9 月 22 日, 24-hour time (14:30).',
	),
	'avoid' => array(
		'English idioms ("hit the ground running" → 迅速上手; "standing on the shoulders of our brands" → 依托旗下众多品牌, never 站在…的肩膀上 unless the object is 巨人).',
	),
	'examples' => array(
		array( 'en' => 'can hold tolerances down to +/- 0.002 mm', 'translation' => '公差可控制在 ±0.002 mm 以内' ),
	),
);
